/-
# Cassels, Chapter 10, §§2–3: the Clifford algebra, its grading and involution, and inner autometries

**Setting.** $k$ a field of characteristic $\ne 2$ (`[Invertible (2 : k)]`), $(V, \phi)$ a finite-dimensional
quadratic space over $k$, written `Q : QuadraticForm k V` ($\phi(\vec x) = Q(\vec x)$; Cassels' bilinear form is
$\phi(\vec x, \vec y) = \tfrac12(\phi(\vec x+\vec y)-\phi(\vec x)-\phi(\vec y))$, Mathlib's `QuadraticMap.associated`).
The Clifford algebra $C(V)$ is Mathlib's `CliffordAlgebra Q`, with the embedding $\iota : V \to C(V)$; Cassels
identifies $\vec x$ with $\iota(\vec x)$. $C_0(V)$, $C_1(V)$ are `evenOdd Q 0`, `evenOdd Q 1`; the even Clifford
algebra is `CliffordAlgebra.even Q`; the canonical involution $u \mapsto u'$ is `CliffordAlgebra.reverse`.

**Proves** (Cassels, *Rational Quadratic Forms*, Ch. 10):
* Lemma 2.1 (p. 171): in a finite-dimensional $k$-algebra a right inverse is a left inverse
  (`mul_eq_one_comm_of_finiteDimensional`), and left and right inverses agree (`eq_of_mul_eq_one_of_mul_eq_one`,
  which holds in any monoid).
* Theorem 2.1 (pp. 172–174): $\iota$ is injective ($V$ is a subspace of $C(V)$, `cliffordι_injective`);
  (i) $\dim C(V) = 2^n$ (`finrank_cliffordAlgebra`); (ii) $C(V)$ is spanned by the products of elements of $V$
  (`iSup_range_ι_pow_eq_top`); (iii) $\vec x\vec x = \phi(\vec x)$ (`ι_mul_ι_self`); uniqueness: any $k$-algebra
  with a linear map from $V$ satisfying (i)–(iii) is isomorphic to $C(V)$ compatibly with $V$
  (`exists_algEquiv_cliffordAlgebra`).
* Lemma 2.2 and Corollary (p. 174): $C_i(V)C_j(V) \subseteq C_{i+j}(V)$ (`evenOdd_mul_evenOdd_le`); the inverse
  of a homogeneous element is homogeneous of the same degree (`mem_evenOdd_of_mul_eq_one`); $C_0(V)$ is a subalgebra
  (`toSubmodule_even`).
* Lemma 2.4 (p. 175): the properties of the canonical involution (`reverse_properties`).
* Lemma 2.5 (p. 175): if $uu' = c \in k^\times$ then $u'u = uu'$ and $u^{-1} = c^{-1}u'$ (`inverse_of_mul_reverse`).
* Lemma 3.1 (p. 175): if $u$ is invertible and $u\vec x u^{-1} \in V$ for all $\vec x \in V$, then
  $T_u : \vec x \mapsto u\vec x u^{-1}$ is an autometry of $V$ (`exists_isometryEquiv_of_conj_mem`). Cassels assumes
  $V$ regular from §3 on; the statement holds without it.
* Lemma 2.3 (p. 174), abstract version (`mem_range_algebraMap_of_even_comm`), from the *twisted centre*
  (`mem_range_algebraMap_of_twisted`): if $e_j\,\alpha(g) = g\,e_j$ for an orthogonal basis of anisotropic $e_j$
  ($\alpha$ the grade involution) then $g \in k$; proof by the projections
  $P_j(z) = \tfrac12(z + \phi(e_j)^{-1}e_j\alpha(z)e_j)$, which keep a basis word if $e_j$ occurs in it an even
  number of times and kill it otherwise, and a word in which every $e_j$ occurs evenly is a scalar. (The library's
  `Lattices.mem_range_algebraMap_of_twisted` is the same argument in coordinates over a number field.)
* §3 (p. 176): the Clifford group (`cliffordGroup`), Cassels' $M_0(V)$ (`M0`), the homomorphism $u \mapsto T_u$
  (`conjHom`, isometries by Lemma 3.1), (3.2) $\vec y\vec x\vec y^{-1} = -\tau_{\vec y}\vec x$ (`vecUnit_conj`), and
  Theorem 3.1 (kernel part): $T_u = 1$ iff $u \in k$ for $u \in M_0(V)$ (`conjHom_eq_one_iff`).
* Lemma 3.2 (p. 178): if $B$ generates the group $G$, the commutator subgroup $G'$ is the normal closure of the
  commutators $[b_1, b_2]$ ($b_j \in B$), i.e. it is generated by their conjugates (`commutator_eq_normalClosure`).

**Proof notes.** The dimension $2^n$ comes from Mathlib's linear isomorphism `CliffordAlgebra.equivExterior` with
the exterior algebra (characteristic $\ne 2$) and the basis of the exterior algebra indexed by the subsets of
$\{0,\dots,n-1\}$ (Cassels builds $C(V)$ on the basis $e(J)$ directly). Lemma 2.1 is Mathlib's Dedekind-finiteness
of Artinian rings. Lemma 2.2's last sentence uses the grade involution: $u$ is even (odd) if and only if it is fixed
(negated) by it. Uniqueness in Theorem 2.1: the universal property gives a surjective algebra map
$C(V) \to C'(V)$, which is bijective since both have dimension $2^n$.
-/
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.CliffordAlgebra.Contraction
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.CliffordAlgebra.Conjugation
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.CliffordAlgebra.Even
import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basis
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Artinian.Module
import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Commutator.Basic
import QuadFormsKB.Citation

open Module CliffordAlgebra
open scoped commutatorElement

namespace QuadFormsKB.Cassels

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

section Inverse

/-- **One-sided inverses are two-sided** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Lemma 2.1, p. 171): in a finite-dimensional algebra
$A$ over a field $k$, if $uv = 1$ then $vu = 1$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Lemma 2.1, p. 171 (existence of the two-sided inverse)"]
theorem mul_eq_one_comm_of_finiteDimensional (k : Type*) {A : Type*} [Field k] [Ring A] [Algebra k A] [FiniteDimensional k A]
    {u v : A} (h : u * v = 1) : v * u = 1 := by
  have : IsArtinianRing A := IsArtinianRing.of_finite k A
  exact mul_eq_one_symm h

/-- **Uniqueness of inverses** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Lemma 2.1, p. 171): if $uv = 1$ and $wu = 1$ then $v = w$
(so both are unique). This holds in any monoid. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Lemma 2.1, p. 171 (v = w, uniqueness)"]
theorem eq_of_mul_eq_one_of_mul_eq_one {A : Type*} [Monoid A] {u v w : A} (hv : u * v = 1) (hw : w * u = 1) : v = w := by
  calc v = (w * u) * v := by rw [hw, one_mul]
    _ = w := by rw [mul_assoc, hv, mul_one]
end Inverse

variable {k V : Type*} [Field k] [Invertible (2 : k)] [AddCommGroup V] [Module k V]
  [FiniteDimensional k V] (Q : QuadraticForm k V)

/-- **$V$ is a subspace of $C(V)$** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Theorem 2.1, p. 172): over a field of characteristic
$\ne 2$ the canonical map $\iota : V \to C(V)$ is injective. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Thm. 2.1, p. 172 (C(V) contains V as a linear subspace)"]
theorem cliffordι_injective : Function.Injective (ι Q) := by
  intro x y h
  have := congrArg (equivExterior Q) h
  simp only [equivExterior, changeFormEquiv_apply, changeForm_ι] at this
  exact (ExteriorAlgebra.ι_inj k x y).1 this

/-- **Dimension of the Clifford algebra** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Theorem 2.1 (i), p. 172): for a quadratic space $V$ of
dimension $n$ over a field of characteristic $\ne 2$, $\dim_k C(V) = 2^n$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Thm. 2.1 (i), p. 172"]
theorem finrank_cliffordAlgebra : finrank k (CliffordAlgebra Q) = 2 ^ finrank k V := by
  rw [(equivExterior Q).finrank_eq,
    finrank_eq_card_basis (Module.finBasis k V).ExteriorAlgebra, Fintype.card_finset,
    Fintype.card_fin]

/-- $C(V)$ is finite-dimensional. -/
instance : FiniteDimensional k (CliffordAlgebra Q) :=
  have : Module.Finite k (ExteriorAlgebra k V) := Module.Finite.of_basis (Module.finBasis k V).ExteriorAlgebra
  Module.Finite.equiv (equivExterior Q).symm


/-- **The defining relation** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Theorem 2.1 (iii), (2.9), p. 172): $\vec x\vec x = \phi(\vec x)$ in
$C(V)$ for every $\vec x \in V$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Thm. 2.1 (iii), (2.9), p. 172"]
theorem ι_mul_ι_self (x : V) : ι Q x * ι Q x = algebraMap k (CliffordAlgebra Q) (Q x) :=
  ι_sq_scalar Q x

/-- **$C(V)$ is spanned by products of vectors** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Theorem 2.1 (ii), p. 172): the subspaces
$V^r$ spanned by the products $\vec x_1\cdots\vec x_r$ ($r \ge 0$; $V^0 = k$) together span $C(V)$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Thm. 2.1 (ii), p. 172"]
theorem iSup_range_ι_pow_eq_top : ⨆ i : ℕ, LinearMap.range (ι Q) ^ i = ⊤ := iSup_ι_range_eq_top Q

/-- **Uniqueness of the Clifford algebra** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Theorem 2.1, final sentence, p. 172): if $A$ is a
$k$-algebra with a linear map $f : V \to A$ such that $f(\vec x)^2 = \phi(\vec x)$ (iii), $\dim_k A = 2^n$ (i), and
$A$ is generated by $f(V)$ (ii), then there is a $k$-algebra isomorphism $e : C(V) \to A$ with
$e(\vec x) = f(\vec x)$ for all $\vec x \in V$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Thm. 2.1, p. 172 (uniqueness of C(V))"]
theorem exists_algEquiv_cliffordAlgebra {A : Type*} [Ring A] [Algebra k A] (f : V →ₗ[k] A)
    (hf : ∀ x, f x * f x = algebraMap k A (Q x)) (hdim : finrank k A = 2 ^ finrank k V)
    (hgen : Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range f) = ⊤) :
    ∃ e : CliffordAlgebra Q ≃ₐ[k] A, ∀ x, e (ι Q x) = f x := by
  set g := CliffordAlgebra.lift Q ⟨f, hf⟩
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective g := by
    rw [← AlgHom.range_eq_top, eq_top_iff, ← hgen, Algebra.adjoin_le_iff]
    rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨ι Q x, by simp [g]⟩
  have hA : FiniteDimensional k A := by
    refine Module.finite_of_finrank_pos ?_
    rw [hdim]; positivity
  have hinj : Function.Injective g.toLinearMap := by
    have := LinearMap.injective_iff_surjective_of_finrank_eq_finrank
      (f := g.toLinearMap) (by rw [finrank_cliffordAlgebra, hdim])
    exact this.2 hsurj
  exact ⟨AlgEquiv.ofBijective g ⟨hinj, hsurj⟩, fun x => by change g (ι Q x) = f x; simp [g]⟩

/-- Characteristic $\ne 2$: $v = -v$ forces $v = 0$. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_eq_neg {v : CliffordAlgebra Q} (h : v = -v) : v = 0 := by
  have h2 : (2 : k) • v = 0 := by rw [two_smul]; nth_rewrite 1 [h]; exact neg_add_cancel v
  exact (smul_eq_zero.1 h2).resolve_left (Invertible.ne_zero (2 : k))

/-- An element fixed by the grade involution is even. -/
theorem mem_even_of_involute_eq {v : CliffordAlgebra Q} (h : involute v = v) : v ∈ evenOdd Q 0 := by
  have htop : v ∈ evenOdd Q 0 ⊔ evenOdd Q 1 := by rw [(evenOdd_isCompl Q).sup_eq_top]; trivial
  obtain ⟨v0, h0, v1, h1, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.1 htop
  rw [map_add, involute_eq_of_mem_even h0, involute_eq_of_mem_odd h1, add_right_inj] at h
  rw [eq_zero_of_eq_neg Q h.symm, add_zero]; exact h0

/-- An element negated by the grade involution is odd. -/
theorem mem_odd_of_involute_eq_neg {v : CliffordAlgebra Q} (h : involute v = -v) :
    v ∈ evenOdd Q 1 := by
  have htop : v ∈ evenOdd Q 0 ⊔ evenOdd Q 1 := by rw [(evenOdd_isCompl Q).sup_eq_top]; trivial
  obtain ⟨v0, h0, v1, h1, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.1 htop
  rw [map_add, involute_eq_of_mem_even h0, involute_eq_of_mem_odd h1, neg_add] at h
  have : v0 = -v0 := by simpa using h
  rw [eq_zero_of_eq_neg Q this, zero_add]; exact h1

/-- **$C(V)$ is graded** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Lemma 2.2, p. 174): $C_i(V)C_j(V) \subseteq C_m(V)$ for
$i, j \in \mathbb Z/2$ and $m = i + j$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Lemma 2.2, p. 174 (first sentence)"]
theorem evenOdd_mul_evenOdd_le (i j : ZMod 2) : evenOdd Q i * evenOdd Q j ≤ evenOdd Q (i + j) :=
  evenOdd_mul_le Q i j

/-- **Inverses of homogeneous elements are homogeneous** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Lemma 2.2, p. 174): if
$u \in C_i(V)$ and $uv = 1$ then $v = u^-1 \in C_i(V)$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Lemma 2.2, p. 174 (second sentence)"]
theorem mem_evenOdd_of_mul_eq_one {i : ZMod 2} {u v : CliffordAlgebra Q} (hu : u ∈ evenOdd Q i)
    (huv : u * v = 1) : v ∈ evenOdd Q i := by
  have hvu : v * u = 1 := mul_eq_one_comm_of_finiteDimensional k huv
  have hinv : involute u * involute v = 1 := by rw [← map_mul, huv, map_one]
  fin_cases i
  · rw [involute_eq_of_mem_even hu] at hinv
    exact mem_even_of_involute_eq Q (eq_of_mul_eq_one_of_mul_eq_one huv (mul_eq_one_comm_of_finiteDimensional k hinv)).symm
  · rw [involute_eq_of_mem_odd hu] at hinv
    have h' : u * (-involute v) = 1 := by rw [mul_neg, ← neg_mul, hinv]
    have := eq_of_mul_eq_one_of_mul_eq_one huv (mul_eq_one_comm_of_finiteDimensional k h')
    refine mem_odd_of_involute_eq_neg Q ?_
    rw [eq_neg_iff_add_eq_zero, add_comm, ← eq_neg_iff_add_eq_zero]; exact this

/-- **The even Clifford algebra** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Lemma 2.2, Corollary, p. 174): $C_0(V)$ is a subalgebra of
$C(V)$: the underlying subspace of the subalgebra `CliffordAlgebra.even Q` is $C_0(V)$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Lemma 2.2, Corollary, p. 174"]
theorem toSubmodule_even : Subalgebra.toSubmodule (even Q) = evenOdd Q 0 := rfl

/-- **The canonical involution** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Lemma 2.4, p. 175): the $k$-linear map $u \mapsto u'$
(`reverse`) satisfies (i) $u' = u$ for $u \in k$ and for $u \in V$, (ii) $(uv)' = v'u'$, (iii) $(u')' = u$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Lemma 2.4, p. 175"]
theorem reverse_properties :
    (∀ c : k, reverse (algebraMap k (CliffordAlgebra Q) c) = algebraMap k _ c) ∧
    (∀ x : V, reverse (ι Q x) = ι Q x) ∧
    (∀ u v : CliffordAlgebra Q, reverse (u * v) = reverse v * reverse u) ∧
    (∀ u : CliffordAlgebra Q, reverse (reverse u) = u) :=
  ⟨reverse.commutes, reverse_ι, reverse.map_mul, reverse_reverse⟩

/-- **Inverse via the involution** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Lemma 2.5, p. 175): if $uu' = c$ with $c \in k^\times$, then
$u'u = c = uu'$ (2.23) and $c^-1u'$ is a two-sided inverse of $u$ (2.24). -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Lemma 2.5, p. 175"]
theorem inverse_of_mul_reverse {u : CliffordAlgebra Q} {c : k} (hc : c ≠ 0)
    (h : u * reverse u = algebraMap k _ c) :
    reverse u * u = algebraMap k _ c ∧ u * (c⁻¹ • reverse u) = 1 ∧ (c⁻¹ • reverse u) * u = 1 := by
  have h1 : u * (c⁻¹ • reverse u) = 1 := by
    rw [mul_smul_comm, h, Algebra.smul_def, ← map_mul, inv_mul_cancel₀ hc, map_one]
  have h2 := mul_eq_one_comm_of_finiteDimensional k h1
  refine ⟨?_, h1, h2⟩
  rw [smul_mul_assoc] at h2
  have := congrArg (fun w => c • w) h2
  simp only [smul_smul, mul_inv_cancel₀ hc, one_smul] at this
  rw [this, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one]

/-- **Inner autometries** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Lemma 3.1, p. 175): if $u \in C(V)$ is invertible and
$u\vec x u^-1 \in V$ for every $\vec x \in V$, then $T_u : \vec x \mapsto u\vec x u^-1$ is an autometry of $V$:
there is an isometry $T$ of $(V,\phi)$ onto itself with $T(\vec x) = u\vec x u^-1$. (Regularity of $V$ is not
needed.) -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Lemma 3.1, p. 175"]
theorem exists_isometryEquiv_of_conj_mem (u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)
    (h : ∀ x : V, ∃ y : V, ι Q y = u * ι Q x * ↑u⁻¹) :
    ∃ T : QuadraticMap.IsometryEquiv Q Q, ∀ x, ι Q (T x) = u * ι Q x * ↑u⁻¹ := by
  choose t ht using h
  let T : V →ₗ[k] V :=
    { toFun := t
      map_add' := fun x y => cliffordι_injective Q (by simp only [map_add, ht, mul_add, add_mul])
      map_smul' := fun c x => cliffordι_injective Q (by
        simp only [map_smul, ht, RingHom.id_apply, mul_smul_comm, smul_mul_assoc]) }
  have hT : Function.Injective T := by
    intro x y hxy
    apply cliffordι_injective Q
    have h1 := ht x; have h2 := ht y
    change t x = t y at hxy
    rw [hxy, h2] at h1
    have := congrArg (fun w => (↑u⁻¹ : CliffordAlgebra Q) * w * u) h1
    simpa [mul_assoc] using this.symm
  have hQ : ∀ x, Q (T x) = Q x := by
    intro x
    apply (algebraMap k (CliffordAlgebra Q)).injective
    rw [← ι_sq_scalar, ← ι_sq_scalar]
    change ι Q (t x) * ι Q (t x) = _
    rw [ht]
    calc (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) * ι Q x * ↑u⁻¹ * (u * ι Q x * ↑u⁻¹)
        = u * (ι Q x * ι Q x) * ↑u⁻¹ := by simp only [mul_assoc, Units.inv_mul_cancel_left]
      _ = ι Q x * ι Q x := by
        rw [ι_sq_scalar, ← Algebra.commutes, mul_assoc, Units.mul_inv, mul_one]
  exact ⟨{ LinearEquiv.ofInjectiveEndo T hT with map_app' := hQ }, ht⟩


/-- **Generators of the commutator subgroup** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Lemma 3.2, p. 178): if the subset $B$
generates the group $G$, then the commutator subgroup $G' = [G, G]$ is the normal closure of the commutators
$[b_1, b_2] = b_1b_2b_1^-1b_2^-1$ with $b_1, b_2 \in B$, i.e. $G'$ is generated by the conjugates
$c[b_1,b_2]c^-1$ ($c \in G$, $b_j \in B$). -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Lemma 3.2, p. 178"]
theorem commutator_eq_normalClosure {G : Type*} [Group G] {B : Set G} (hB : Subgroup.closure B = ⊤) :
    commutator G = Subgroup.normalClosure {g : G | ∃ b₁ ∈ B, ∃ b₂ ∈ B, g = ⁅b₁, b₂⁆} := by
  set N := Subgroup.normalClosure {g : G | ∃ b₁ ∈ B, ∃ b₂ ∈ B, g = ⁅b₁, b₂⁆}
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · -- generators commute modulo `N`
    have hcomm : ∀ b₁ ∈ B, ∀ b₂ ∈ B, Commute (QuotientGroup.mk' N b₁) (QuotientGroup.mk' N b₂) := by
      intro b₁ h₁ b₂ h₂
      have hm : (⁅b₁, b₂⁆ : G) ∈ N := Subgroup.subset_normalClosure ⟨b₁, h₁, b₂, h₂, rfl⟩
      have : QuotientGroup.mk' N (⁅b₁, b₂⁆ : G) = 1 := (QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff _).2 hm
      rw [map_commutatorElement, commutatorElement_eq_one_iff_commute] at this
      exact this
    have key : ∀ g h : G, Commute (QuotientGroup.mk' N g) (QuotientGroup.mk' N h) := by
      have step : ∀ x : G ⧸ N, (∀ b ∈ B, Commute x (QuotientGroup.mk' N b)) →
          ∀ h : G, Commute x (QuotientGroup.mk' N h) := by
        intro x hx h
        have hle : Subgroup.closure B ≤ (Subgroup.centralizer {x}).comap (QuotientGroup.mk' N) := by
          rw [Subgroup.closure_le]
          intro b hb
          simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, Subgroup.mem_comap, Subgroup.mem_centralizer_singleton_iff]
          exact (hx b hb).symm
        have := hle (hB ▸ Subgroup.mem_top h)
        simp only [Subgroup.mem_comap, Subgroup.mem_centralizer_singleton_iff] at this
        exact this.symm
      intro g h
      refine step _ ?_ h
      intro b hb
      exact (step _ (fun b' hb' => hcomm b hb b' hb') g).symm
    rw [commutator, Subgroup.commutator_le]
    intro g _ h _
    rw [← QuotientGroup.eq_one_iff]
    change QuotientGroup.mk' N ⁅g, h⁆ = 1
    rw [map_commutatorElement, commutatorElement_eq_one_iff_commute]
    exact key g h
  · refine Subgroup.normalClosure_le_normal ?_
    rintro _ ⟨b₁, -, b₂, -, rfl⟩
    exact Subgroup.commutator_mem_commutator (Subgroup.mem_top b₁) (Subgroup.mem_top b₂)

section Center

variable {k V : Type*} [Field k] [Invertible (2 : k)] [AddCommGroup V] [Module k V]
  (Q : QuadraticForm k V) {n : ℕ} (e : Basis (Fin n) k V)

/-- The basis word $e_{j_1}\cdots e_{j_r}$ in $C(V)$. -/
noncomputable def bword (l : List (Fin n)) : CliffordAlgebra Q := (l.map fun i => ι Q (e i)).prod

theorem bword_nil : bword Q e [] = 1 := rfl

theorem bword_cons (i : Fin n) (l : List (Fin n)) : bword Q e (i :: l) = ι Q (e i) * bword Q e l := by
  simp [bword]

theorem bword_append (l₁ l₂ : List (Fin n)) : bword Q e (l₁ ++ l₂) = bword Q e l₁ * bword Q e l₂ := by
  simp [bword]

theorem mem_span_bword (z : CliffordAlgebra Q) : z ∈ Submodule.span k (Set.range (bword Q e)) := by
  induction z using CliffordAlgebra.induction with
  | algebraMap r =>
    rw [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨[], rfl⟩)
  | ι x =>
    rw [← e.sum_repr x, map_sum]
    refine Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i _ => ?_
    rw [map_smul]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨[i], by simp [bword]⟩)
  | mul a b ha hb =>
    refine Submodule.span_induction (p := fun a _ => a * b ∈ Submodule.span k (Set.range (bword Q e)))
      ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ ha
    · rintro _ ⟨l₁, rfl⟩
      refine Submodule.span_induction
        (p := fun b _ => bword Q e l₁ * b ∈ Submodule.span k (Set.range (bword Q e))) ?_ ?_ ?_ ?_ hb
      · rintro _ ⟨l₂, rfl⟩
        exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨l₁ ++ l₂, bword_append Q e l₁ l₂⟩
      · simp
      · intro x y _ _ h1 h2; rw [mul_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ h1 h2
      · intro r x _ h; rw [mul_smul_comm]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ h
    · simp
    · intro x y _ _ h1 h2; rw [add_mul]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ h1 h2
    · intro r x _ h; rw [smul_mul_assoc]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ h
  | add a b ha hb => exact Submodule.add_mem _ ha hb

theorem neg_one_pow_sq_eq (m : ℕ) : ((-1 : k) ^ m) ^ 2 = 1 := by
  rw [← pow_mul, mul_comm, pow_mul]; simp

variable {Q e}
variable (horth : ∀ i j, i ≠ j → QuadraticMap.polar Q (e i) (e j) = 0)
include horth

theorem ι_anticomm {i j : Fin n} (h : i ≠ j) : ι Q (e j) * ι Q (e i) = -(ι Q (e i) * ι Q (e j)) := by
  have := ι_mul_ι_add_swap (Q := Q) (e j) (e i)
  rw [horth j i h.symm, map_zero] at this
  exact eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_left this

theorem ι_mul_bword (j : Fin n) (l : List (Fin n)) :
    ι Q (e j) * bword Q e l = (-1 : k) ^ (l.length + l.count j) • (bword Q e l * ι Q (e j)) := by
  induction l with
  | nil => simp [bword]
  | cons i l ih =>
    rw [bword_cons]
    by_cases hij : i = j
    · subst hij
      rw [← mul_assoc, ι_sq_scalar, ih, smul_mul_assoc, mul_assoc, ι_sq_scalar, ← Algebra.commutes,
        ← Algebra.smul_def]
      rw [smul_smul, smul_smul]
      simp only [List.length_cons, List.count_cons_self]
      congr 1
      ring_nf
      rw [pow_mul, pow_mul, neg_one_pow_sq_eq, neg_one_pow_sq_eq]; ring
    · rw [← mul_assoc, ι_anticomm horth hij, neg_mul, mul_assoc, ih, mul_smul_comm, ← mul_assoc,
        ← neg_smul]
      simp only [List.length_cons, List.count_cons, beq_iff_eq, hij, ite_false, add_zero, mul_assoc]
      congr 1
      ring

omit horth in
theorem involute_bword (l : List (Fin n)) :
    involute (bword Q e l) = (-1 : k) ^ l.length • bword Q e l := by
  induction l with
  | nil => simp [bword]
  | cons i l ih =>
    rw [bword_cons, map_mul, involute_ι, ih, neg_mul, mul_smul_comm, ← neg_smul, List.length_cons, pow_succ]
    congr 1; ring

theorem bword_mem_range_of_even :
    ∀ m : ℕ, ∀ l : List (Fin n), l.length = m → (∀ j, Even (l.count j)) →
      bword Q e l ∈ Set.range (algebraMap k (CliffordAlgebra Q)) := by
  intro m
  induction m using Nat.strong_induction_on with
  | _ m ih =>
    intro l hl hev
    match l with
    | [] => exact ⟨1, by simp [bword]⟩
    | i :: l' =>
      have hodd : 0 < l'.count i := by
        have := hev i
        rw [List.count_cons_self] at this
        rcases Nat.even_or_odd (l'.count i) with h | h
        · exact absurd this (by rw [Nat.even_add_one]; exact not_not.2 h)
        · exact h.pos
      obtain ⟨s, t, rfl⟩ := List.append_of_mem (List.count_pos_iff.1 hodd)
      have hev' : ∀ j, Even ((s ++ t).count j) := by
        intro j
        have := hev j
        simp only [List.count_cons, List.count_append, beq_iff_eq] at this ⊢
        by_cases hj : i = j
        · subst hj; simp only [ite_true] at this
          have h2 : List.count i s + List.count i t + 2 = List.count i s + (List.count i t + 1) + 1 := by
            ring
          rw [← h2] at this
          exact (Nat.even_add.1 this).2 even_two
        · simpa [hj] using this
      obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := ih (s ++ t).length (by simp [← hl]) (s ++ t) rfl hev'
      refine ⟨(-1 : k) ^ (s.length + s.count i) * Q (e i) * c, ?_⟩
      have e1 : ι Q (e i) * (bword Q e s * (ι Q (e i) * bword Q e t)) =
          (-1 : k) ^ (s.length + s.count i) • (Q (e i) • (bword Q e s * bword Q e t)) := by
        rw [← mul_assoc, ι_mul_bword horth, smul_mul_assoc, mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc (ι Q (e i)),
          ι_sq_scalar, ← Algebra.smul_def, mul_smul_comm]
      rw [bword_cons, bword_append, bword_cons, e1, ← bword_append, ← hc]
      simp only [Algebra.smul_def, map_mul, mul_assoc]

omit horth in
/-- The projection $P_j(z) = \tfrac12\bigl(z + \phi(e_j)^{-1}e_j\,\alpha(z)\,e_j\bigr)$. -/
noncomputable def projP (j : Fin n) : CliffordAlgebra Q →ₗ[k] CliffordAlgebra Q :=
  (⅟2 : k) • (LinearMap.id + (Q (e j))⁻¹ •
    ((LinearMap.mulLeft k (ι Q (e j))).comp ((LinearMap.mulRight k (ι Q (e j))).comp
      (involute : CliffordAlgebra Q →ₐ[k] CliffordAlgebra Q).toLinearMap)))

omit horth in
theorem projP_apply (j : Fin n) (z : CliffordAlgebra Q) :
    projP (Q := Q) (e := e) j z =
      (⅟2 : k) • (z + (Q (e j))⁻¹ • (ι Q (e j) * (involute z * ι Q (e j)))) := by
  simp [projP]

theorem projP_bword (hne : ∀ i, Q (e i) ≠ 0) (j : Fin n) (l : List (Fin n)) :
    projP (Q := Q) (e := e) j (bword Q e l) = if Even (l.count j) then bword Q e l else 0 := by
  rw [projP_apply, involute_bword, smul_mul_assoc, mul_smul_comm, ← mul_assoc, ι_mul_bword horth,
    smul_mul_assoc, mul_assoc, ι_sq_scalar, ← Algebra.commutes, ← Algebra.smul_def, smul_smul, smul_smul,
    smul_smul, inv_mul_eq_div]
  have hs : (-1 : k) ^ l.length * (-1) ^ (l.length + l.count j) = (-1) ^ l.count j := by
    rw [pow_add, ← mul_assoc, ← pow_add, ← two_mul, pow_mul]; simp
  have hc : (-1 : k) ^ l.length / Q (e j) * (-1) ^ (l.length + l.count j) * Q (e j) = (-1) ^ l.count j := by
    rw [← hs]; field_simp [hne j]
  rw [hc]
  split_ifs with h
  · rw [h.neg_one_pow, one_smul, ← two_smul k, smul_smul, invOf_mul_self, one_smul]
  · rw [Nat.not_even_iff_odd.1 h |>.neg_one_pow, neg_one_smul, add_neg_cancel, smul_zero]

theorem projP_of_twisted (hne : ∀ i, Q (e i) ≠ 0) (j : Fin n) {g : CliffordAlgebra Q}
    (hg : ι Q (e j) * involute g = g * ι Q (e j)) : projP (Q := Q) (e := e) j g = g := by
  rw [projP_apply, ← mul_assoc, hg, mul_assoc, ι_sq_scalar, ← Algebra.commutes, ← Algebra.smul_def, smul_smul,
    inv_mul_cancel₀ (hne j), one_smul, ← two_smul k, smul_smul, invOf_mul_self, one_smul]

/-- **The twisted centre of $C(V)$ is $k$.** -/
theorem mem_range_algebraMap_of_twisted (hne : ∀ i, Q (e i) ≠ 0) {g : CliffordAlgebra Q}
    (hg : ∀ j, ι Q (e j) * involute g = g * ι Q (e j)) :
    g ∈ Set.range (algebraMap k (CliffordAlgebra Q)) := by
  let S : ℕ → Submodule k (CliffordAlgebra Q) := fun m =>
    Submodule.span k {w | ∃ l : List (Fin n), (∀ j : Fin n, j.val < m → Even (l.count j)) ∧ bword Q e l = w}
  have step : ∀ m ≤ n, g ∈ S m := by
    intro m
    induction m with
    | zero =>
      intro _
      refine Submodule.span_mono ?_ (mem_span_bword Q e g)
      rintro _ ⟨l, rfl⟩; exact ⟨l, fun j hj => absurd hj (Nat.not_lt_zero _), rfl⟩
    | succ m ih =>
      intro hm
      have hg' := ih (by omega)
      rw [← projP_of_twisted horth hne ⟨m, by omega⟩ (hg _)]
      have : (S m).map (projP (Q := Q) (e := e) ⟨m, by omega⟩) ≤ S (m + 1) := by
        rw [Submodule.map_span, Submodule.span_le]
        rintro _ ⟨_, ⟨l, hl, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
        rw [projP_bword horth hne]
        split_ifs with h
        · refine Submodule.subset_span ⟨l, fun j hj => ?_, rfl⟩
          rcases Nat.lt_succ_iff_lt_or_eq.1 hj with hj | hj
          · exact hl j hj
          · have : j = ⟨m, by omega⟩ := Fin.ext hj
            exact this ▸ h
        · exact Submodule.zero_mem _
      exact this (Submodule.mem_map_of_mem hg')
  have hfin := step n le_rfl
  have hle : S n ≤ LinearMap.range (Algebra.linearMap k (CliffordAlgebra Q)) := by
    rw [Submodule.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨l, hl, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := bword_mem_range_of_even horth l.length l rfl (fun j => hl j j.isLt)
    exact ⟨c, hc⟩
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hle hfin
  exact ⟨c, hc⟩

end Center


section Spin

variable {k V : Type*} [Field k] [Invertible (2 : k)] [AddCommGroup V] [Module k V]
  [FiniteDimensional k V] {Q : QuadraticForm k V}

/-- A regular space has an orthogonal basis of anisotropic vectors. -/
theorem exists_orthogonal_basis_aniso (hQ : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).Nondegenerate) :
    ∃ e : Basis (Fin (finrank k V)) k V, (∀ i j, i ≠ j → QuadraticMap.polar Q (e i) (e j) = 0) ∧
      ∀ i, Q (e i) ≠ 0 := by
  obtain ⟨v, hv⟩ := LinearMap.BilinForm.exists_orthogonal_basis (QuadraticForm.associated_isSymm k Q)
  refine ⟨v, fun i j hij => ?_, fun i => ?_⟩
  · have h : QuadraticMap.associated Q (v i) (v j) = 0 := hv hij
    have := congrArg (fun B : LinearMap.BilinForm k V => B (v i) (v j))
      (QuadraticMap.two_nsmul_associated (S := k) (Q := Q))
    simp only [LinearMap.smul_apply, QuadraticMap.polarBilin_apply_apply] at this
    rw [← this]
    change 2 • QuadraticMap.associated Q (v i) (v j) = 0
    rw [h, smul_zero]
  · have h := hv.not_isOrtho_basis_self_of_separatingLeft hQ.1 i
    rwa [QuadraticMap.associated_eq_self_apply] at h

/-- Twisted commutation with all of $V$ forces a scalar (regular $V$). -/
theorem mem_range_algebraMap_of_twisted' (hQ : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).Nondegenerate)
    {g : CliffordAlgebra Q} (hg : ∀ x, ι Q x * involute g = g * ι Q x) :
    g ∈ Set.range (algebraMap k (CliffordAlgebra Q)) := by
  obtain ⟨e, horth, hne⟩ := exists_orthogonal_basis_aniso hQ
  exact mem_range_algebraMap_of_twisted horth hne fun j => hg (e j)

/-- **Cassels, Ch. 10, Lemma 2.3, p. 174 (abstract version).** For a regular quadratic space $V$ (characteristic
$\ne 2$), an element $u \in C_0(V)$ that commutes with every $\vec x \in V$ lies in $k$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Lemma 2.3, p. 174 (abstract quadratic space over any field of characteristic ≠ 2)"]
theorem mem_range_algebraMap_of_even_comm (hQ : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).Nondegenerate) {u : CliffordAlgebra Q}
    (hu : u ∈ evenOdd Q 0) (hc : ∀ x, u * ι Q x = ι Q x * u) :
    u ∈ Set.range (algebraMap k (CliffordAlgebra Q)) :=
  mem_range_algebraMap_of_twisted' hQ fun x => by rw [involute_eq_of_mem_even hu, hc]

theorem eq_zero_of_odd_anticomm (hQ : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).Nondegenerate) {u : CliffordAlgebra Q}
    (hu : u ∈ evenOdd Q 1) (hc : ∀ x, u * ι Q x = -(ι Q x * u)) : u = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := mem_range_algebraMap_of_twisted' hQ fun x => by
    rw [involute_eq_of_mem_odd hu, mul_neg, hc]
  have h0 : algebraMap k (CliffordAlgebra Q) c ∈ evenOdd Q 0 := by
    rw [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one]
    exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (one_le_evenOdd_zero Q (Submodule.mem_one.2 ⟨1, by simp⟩))
  have := (evenOdd_isCompl Q).disjoint
  rw [Submodule.disjoint_def] at this
  exact this _ h0 hu

variable (Q) in
/-- **Cassels' group $M_0(V)$** (Ch. 10, §3, p. 176): the invertible $u \in C_0(V)$ with $u\vec x u^{-1} \in V$ for
all $\vec x \in V$. -/
def M0 : Subgroup (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ where
  carrier := {u | (u : CliffordAlgebra Q) ∈ evenOdd Q 0 ∧ ∀ x, ∃ y, ι Q y = u * ι Q x * ↑u⁻¹}
  one_mem' := ⟨one_le_evenOdd_zero Q (Submodule.mem_one.2 ⟨1, by simp⟩), fun x => ⟨x, by simp⟩⟩
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro u v ⟨hu, hu'⟩ ⟨hv, hv'⟩
    refine ⟨by simpa using SetLike.mul_mem_graded hu hv, fun x => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hv' x
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hu' y
    exact ⟨z, by rw [hz, hy]; simp [mul_assoc]⟩
  inv_mem' := by
    rintro u ⟨hu, hu'⟩
    refine ⟨mem_evenOdd_of_mul_eq_one Q hu u.mul_inv, fun x => ?_⟩
    -- `y ↦ u y u⁻¹` is an injective endomorphism of `V`, hence surjective
    choose t ht using hu'
    let T : V →ₗ[k] V :=
      { toFun := t
        map_add' := fun x y => cliffordι_injective Q (by simp only [map_add, ht, mul_add, add_mul])
        map_smul' := fun c x => cliffordι_injective Q (by
          simp only [map_smul, ht, RingHom.id_apply, mul_smul_comm, smul_mul_assoc]) }
    have hT : Function.Injective T := by
      intro x y hxy
      apply cliffordι_injective Q
      have h1 := ht x; have h2 := ht y
      change t x = t y at hxy
      rw [hxy, h2] at h1
      have := congrArg (fun w => (↑u⁻¹ : CliffordAlgebra Q) * w * u) h1
      simpa [mul_assoc] using this.symm
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := LinearMap.surjective_of_injective hT x
    refine ⟨y, ?_⟩
    have := ht y
    change t y = x at hy
    rw [hy] at this
    rw [this]; simp [mul_assoc]

theorem M0_conj {u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ} (hu : u ∈ M0 Q) (x : V) :
    ∃ y, ι Q y = u * ι Q x * ↑u⁻¹ := hu.2 x

/-- If $u\vec x u^{-1} \in V$ for every $\vec x$, the map $\vec x \mapsto u\vec x u^{-1}$ is a bijection of $V$. -/
theorem conj_bijective {u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ} (h : ∀ x, ∃ y, ι Q y = u * ι Q x * ↑u⁻¹) :
    ∃ T : V ≃ₗ[k] V, ∀ x, ι Q (T x) = u * ι Q x * ↑u⁻¹ := by
  choose t ht using h
  let T : V →ₗ[k] V :=
    { toFun := t
      map_add' := fun x y => cliffordι_injective Q (by simp only [map_add, ht, mul_add, add_mul])
      map_smul' := fun c x => cliffordι_injective Q (by
        simp only [map_smul, ht, RingHom.id_apply, mul_smul_comm, smul_mul_assoc]) }
  have hT : Function.Injective T := by
    intro x y hxy
    apply cliffordι_injective Q
    have h1 := ht x; have h2 := ht y
    change t x = t y at hxy
    rw [hxy, h2] at h1
    have := congrArg (fun w => (↑u⁻¹ : CliffordAlgebra Q) * w * u) h1
    simpa [mul_assoc] using this.symm
  exact ⟨LinearEquiv.ofInjectiveEndo T hT, ht⟩

variable (Q) in
/-- **The Clifford group**: the units $u$ of $C(V)$ with $u V u^{-1} \subseteq V$. -/
def cliffordGroup : Subgroup (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ where
  carrier := {u | ∀ x, ∃ y, ι Q y = u * ι Q x * ↑u⁻¹}
  one_mem' := fun x => ⟨x, by simp⟩
  mul_mem' := by
    rintro u v hu hv x
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hv x
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hu y
    exact ⟨z, by rw [hz, hy]; simp [mul_assoc]⟩
  inv_mem' := by
    rintro u hu x
    obtain ⟨T, hT⟩ := conj_bijective hu
    refine ⟨T.symm x, ?_⟩
    have := hT (T.symm x)
    rw [LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply] at this
    rw [this]; simp [mul_assoc]

theorem M0_le : M0 Q ≤ cliffordGroup Q := fun _ hu => hu.2

/-- **The map $u \mapsto T_u$** (Cassels (3.1)) on the Clifford group, a homomorphism to $GL(V)$. -/
noncomputable def conjHom : cliffordGroup Q →* (V ≃ₗ[k] V) where
  toFun u := (conj_bijective u.2).choose
  map_one' := by
    ext x; apply cliffordι_injective Q
    rw [(conj_bijective (Subgroup.one_mem _ : (1 : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) ∈ cliffordGroup Q)).choose_spec]
    simp
  map_mul' u v := by
    ext x; apply cliffordι_injective Q
    rw [(conj_bijective (u * v).2).choose_spec, LinearEquiv.mul_apply, (conj_bijective u.2).choose_spec,
      (conj_bijective v.2).choose_spec]
    simp [mul_assoc]

theorem conjHom_spec (u : cliffordGroup Q) (x : V) :
    ι Q (conjHom u x) = ((u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) * ι Q x * ↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)⁻¹ :=
  (conj_bijective u.2).choose_spec x

theorem conjHom_isometry (u : cliffordGroup Q) (x : V) : Q (conjHom u x) = Q x := by
  apply (algebraMap k (CliffordAlgebra Q)).injective
  rw [← ι_sq_scalar, ← ι_sq_scalar, conjHom_spec]
  calc ((u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) * ι Q x * ↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)⁻¹ *
        (((u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) * ι Q x * ↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)⁻¹)
      = ((u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) * (ι Q x * ι Q x) * ↑(u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ)⁻¹ := by
        simp only [mul_assoc, Units.inv_mul_cancel_left]
    _ = ι Q x * ι Q x := by
      rw [ι_sq_scalar, ← Algebra.commutes, mul_assoc, Units.mul_inv, mul_one]

/-- **The kernel of $u \mapsto T_u$ on $M_0(V)$ is $k^\times$** (Cassels, Ch. 10, Theorem 3.1, p. 176, via Lemma
2.3): for a regular space and $u$ in the Clifford group with $u \in C_0(V)$, $T_u = 1$ if and only if $u \in k$. -/
@[kb "cassels1978" "Ch. 10, Thm. 3.1, p. 176 (the kernel of u ↦ T_u on M₀(V) is k^×)"]
theorem conjHom_eq_one_iff (hQ : (QuadraticMap.associated Q).Nondegenerate) {u : cliffordGroup Q}
    (hu : ((u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) ∈ evenOdd Q 0) :
    conjHom u = 1 ↔ ((u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) ∈ Set.range (algebraMap k (CliffordAlgebra Q)) := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    refine mem_range_algebraMap_of_even_comm hQ hu fun x => ?_
    have := conjHom_spec u x
    rw [h] at this; change ι Q x = _ at this
    have := congrArg (· * ((u : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q)) this
    simpa [mul_assoc] using this.symm
  · rintro ⟨c, hc⟩
    ext x; apply cliffordι_injective Q
    rw [conjHom_spec, ← hc, Algebra.commutes, hc, mul_assoc]
    simp

/-- An anisotropic vector $\vec y$ is a unit of $C(V)$, with $\vec y^{-1} = \phi(\vec y)^{-1}\vec y$. -/
noncomputable def vecUnit (y : V) (hy : Q y ≠ 0) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ where
  val := ι Q y
  inv := (Q y)⁻¹ • ι Q y
  val_inv := by
    rw [mul_smul_comm, ι_sq_scalar, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, smul_smul, inv_mul_cancel₀ hy, one_smul]
  inv_val := by
    rw [smul_mul_assoc, ι_sq_scalar, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, smul_smul, inv_mul_cancel₀ hy, one_smul]

/-- $\vec y\vec x\vec y^{-1} = -\tau_{\vec y}\vec x$ (Cassels (3.2)), with
$\tau_{\vec y}\vec x = \vec x - \frac{\phi(\vec x+\vec y)-\phi(\vec x)-\phi(\vec y)}{\phi(\vec y)}\vec y$. -/
theorem vecUnit_conj (y : V) (hy : Q y ≠ 0) (x : V) :
    ((vecUnit y hy : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) * ι Q x * ↑(vecUnit y hy)⁻¹ =
      ι Q (-(x - (QuadraticMap.polar Q x y / Q y) • y)) := by
  change ι Q y * ι Q x * ((Q y)⁻¹ • ι Q y) = _
  have h := ι_mul_ι_add_swap (Q := Q) y x
  have e1 : ι Q y * ι Q x = algebraMap k _ (QuadraticMap.polar Q y x) - ι Q x * ι Q y := eq_sub_of_add_eq h
  rw [mul_smul_comm, e1, sub_mul, mul_assoc, ι_sq_scalar, ← Algebra.commutes, ← Algebra.smul_def,
    ← Algebra.smul_def, QuadraticMap.polar_comm, smul_sub, smul_smul, smul_smul, inv_mul_cancel₀ hy, one_smul]
  simp only [map_neg, map_sub, map_smul]
  rw [div_eq_inv_mul, neg_sub]

theorem vecUnit_mem (y : V) (hy : Q y ≠ 0) : vecUnit y hy ∈ cliffordGroup Q :=
  fun x => ⟨_, (vecUnit_conj y hy x).symm⟩

theorem conjHom_vecUnit (y : V) (hy : Q y ≠ 0) (x : V) :
    conjHom ⟨vecUnit y hy, vecUnit_mem y hy⟩ x = -(x - (QuadraticMap.polar Q x y / Q y) • y) :=
  cliffordι_injective Q (by rw [conjHom_spec]; exact vecUnit_conj y hy x)

/-- The product $\vec y_1\cdots\vec y_r$ of anisotropic vectors, as an element of the Clifford group. -/
noncomputable def vecProd (l : List V) (hl : ∀ y ∈ l, Q y ≠ 0) : cliffordGroup Q :=
  (l.attach.map fun y => (⟨vecUnit y.1 (hl y.1 y.2), vecUnit_mem _ _⟩ : cliffordGroup Q)).prod

theorem vecProd_cons (y : V) (l : List V) (hl : ∀ z ∈ y :: l, Q z ≠ 0) :
    vecProd (y :: l) hl = ⟨vecUnit y (hl y (List.mem_cons_self ..)), vecUnit_mem _ _⟩ *
      vecProd l (fun z hz => hl z (List.mem_cons_of_mem y hz)) := by
  simp only [vecProd, List.attach_cons, List.map_cons, List.prod_cons, List.map_map]
  rfl

theorem coe_vecProd_cons (y : V) (l : List V) (hl : ∀ z ∈ y :: l, Q z ≠ 0) :
    (((vecProd (y :: l) hl : cliffordGroup Q) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) =
      ι Q y * (((vecProd l (fun z hz => hl z (List.mem_cons_of_mem y hz)) : cliffordGroup Q) :
        (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) := by
  rw [vecProd_cons]; rfl

theorem vecProd_mem_evenOdd (l : List V) (hl : ∀ y ∈ l, Q y ≠ 0) :
    (((vecProd l hl : cliffordGroup Q) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) ∈
      evenOdd Q (l.length : ZMod 2) := by
  induction l with
  | nil =>
    simp only [vecProd, List.attach_nil, List.map_nil, List.prod_nil, List.length_nil, Nat.cast_zero]
    exact one_le_evenOdd_zero Q (Submodule.mem_one.2 ⟨1, by simp⟩)
  | cons y l ih =>
    rw [coe_vecProd_cons, List.length_cons, Nat.cast_succ, add_comm]
    exact SetLike.mul_mem_graded (ι_mem_evenOdd_one Q y) (ih _)

theorem vecProd_mul_reverse (l : List V) (hl : ∀ y ∈ l, Q y ≠ 0) :
    (((vecProd l hl : cliffordGroup Q) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) *
      reverse (((vecProd l hl : cliffordGroup Q) : (CliffordAlgebra Q)ˣ) : CliffordAlgebra Q) =
      algebraMap k _ (l.map Q).prod := by
  induction l with
  | nil => simp [vecProd]
  | cons y l ih =>
    rw [coe_vecProd_cons, reverse.map_mul, reverse_ι, mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc _ (reverse _), ih,
      Algebra.commutes, ← mul_assoc, ι_sq_scalar, ← map_mul, List.map_cons, List.prod_cons]

end Spin

